      "type": "model",
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Let me work through the mathematics carefully before submitting.\n\n**Part (1):** Given $\\frac{a_{n+1}}{n} = \\frac{a_n}{n+1} + \\frac{1}{n(n+1)}$.\n\nMultiply both sides by $n(n+1)$: $(n+1)a_{n+1} = n a_n + 1$.\n\nSo $(n+1)a_{n+1} - n a_n = 1$, a constant. Thus $\\{n a_n\\}$ is arithmetic with common difference 1.\n\n**Part (2):** $b_n = n a_n$ is arithmetic with $b_1 = 1\\cdot a_1 = 3$, difference $d=1$, so $b_n = 3 + (n-1) = n+2$. Hence $a_n = \\frac{n+2}{n} = 1 + \\frac{2}{n}$.\n\n$f(x) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} a_k x^k$, so $f'(x) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} k a_k x^{k-1} = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} (k+2) x^{k-1}$.\n\nAt $x=-2$: $f'(-2) = \\sum_{k=1}^{m} (k+2)(-2)^{k-1}$.\n\nLet $j = k-1$, $k = j+1$: $= \\sum_{j=0}^{m-1} (j+3)(-2)^j = \\sum_{j=0}^{m-1} j(-2)^j + 3\\sum_{j=0}^{m-1}(-2)^j$.\n\n$\\sum_{j=0}^{m-1}(-2)^j = \\frac{1-(-2)^m}{1-(-2)} = \\frac{1-(-2)^m}{3}$.\n\n$\\sum_{j=0}^{m-1} j(-2)^j$: use $\\sum_{j=0}^{n} j r^j = \\frac{r - (n+1)r^{n+1} + n r^{n+2}}{(1-r)^2}$ with $r=-2$, $n=m-1$:\n$= \\frac{-2 - m(-2)^m + (m-1)(-2)^{m+1}}{9} = \\frac{-2 - m(-2)^m - 2(m-1)(-2)^m}{9} = \\frac{-2 - (3m-2)(-2)^m}{9}$.\n\nSo $f'(-2) = \\frac{-2 - (3m-2)(-2)^m}{9} + 3\\cdot\\frac{1-(-2)^m}{3} = \\frac{-2 - (3m-2)(-2)^m}{9} + \\frac{3 - 3(-2)^m}{3}$.\n\n$= \\frac{-2 - (3m-2)(-2)^m + 9 - 9(-2)^m}{9} = \\frac{7 - (3m+7)(-2)^m}{9}$.\n\nLet me verify with small $m$: $m=1$: $f'(x)=a_1=3$, so $f'(-2)=3$. Formula: $\\frac{7-(3+7)(-2)}{9}=\\frac{7+20}{9}=3$. ✓\n$m=2$: $f'(x)=a_1+2a_2 x = 3 + 2\\cdot 2 x = 3+4x$, at $-2$: $3-8=-5$. Formula: $\\frac{7-(6+7)\\cdot 4}{9}=\\frac{7-52}{9}=-5$. ✓",
        "tool_calls": [
